1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:04,990
You must find your soulmate
from your past life.

2
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:08,300
Then you must marry that person
with heaven and earth as witnesses.

3
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:09,180
Otherwise,

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,680
- this misfortune will follow you
- (Inspector, hang in there.)

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,940
until the day you die.

6
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:14,600
Please help this handsome
but cursed Inspector.

7
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:15,720
After the ceremony is over,

8
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:20,570
you two must share a bed

9
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,550
and become one
in the most intimate way.

10
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:25,990
Why don't you try calling me...

11
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:28,880
husband?

12
00:00:57,170 --> 00:01:00,970
(Wow, his skin is so smooth and radiant.)

13
00:01:00,990 --> 00:01:02,410
(His lips are pink.)

14
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:04,150
(Did he really get commando training?)

15
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:06,090
You're probably thinking...

16
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:09,370
"How does he look this good
even in his sleep?" Right?

17
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:15,280
Don't you put any ideas
in my head.

18
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:20,380
Why don't you come cuddle with me
if you wanna get a closer look?

19
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,000
No thanks.

20
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:24,770
It's warmer down here.

21
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:33,020
Morning.

22
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:35,230
Hey.

23
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:36,490
What?

24
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,480
Oh?

25
00:01:43,450 --> 00:01:44,520
Good morning, Mom.

26
00:01:44,970 --> 00:01:46,730
How was it, Thear?

27
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:49,460
Was it comfortable
sleeping on the floor?

28
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:53,040
It was fine. Quite nice, actually.

29
00:01:55,110 --> 00:01:57,450
Mungkorn, now that you're up,
go take a shower.

30
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,500
Khaomao and Khaopuk
have prepared your breakfast.

31
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:01,690
I need to talk to Thear.

32
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:02,510
Yes.

33
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:18,120
What a wonderful morning.

34
00:02:20,490 --> 00:02:21,780
- Come here.
- Mom.

35
00:02:22,690 --> 00:02:23,290
- Mom.
- I know

36
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:25,220
that you didn't
share the bed with him.

37
00:02:25,730 --> 00:02:26,340
That hurts.

38
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,950
Sh*t, it's hot!

39
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:34,440
It's super hot.

40
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:36,670
Did my balls just get burned?

41
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:37,620
Ow!

42
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,700
Is the water too hot for you?

43
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,470
What are you doing in here?

44
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:50,450
I'm in the bathroom,
so I'm here to take a shower.

45
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:52,630
But I'm taking a shower.

46
00:02:52,950 --> 00:02:56,160
Oh, can't I just join you?

47
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:57,390
Or is it because...

48
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,780
Are you afraid I'll see your willy?

49
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:07,870
You're acting like you've never had
a communal shower during training.

50
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:09,670
This is different.

51
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:11,250
You're right.

52
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:14,730
Because we're husbands now,
aren't we?

53
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,260
The hot water is on that side.

54
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:30,500
And the cold water is over here.

55
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:35,380
Thanks.

56
00:03:35,410 --> 00:03:37,050
You'd better get used to it.

57
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:38,310
I mean my body.

58
00:03:40,430 --> 00:03:43,550
Because we'll be living like this
for another six months.

59
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:53,050
Here is...

60
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:54,210
my chest.

61
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,570
And this part...

62
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:08,860
Inspector!

63
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:10,860
Stop messing around.

64
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,840
Get out now. I need to shower.

65
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:16,420
I've never been with anyone like this.

66
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,690
So give me time to get used to it.

67
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:21,220
Fine. I'll go.

68
00:04:21,490 --> 00:04:23,790
If you need any help, just let me know.

69
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:28,750
If you want me to help scrub or
rub any nooks and crannies...

70
00:04:28,830 --> 00:04:30,700
- I can help...
- Just get out.

71
00:04:35,510 --> 00:04:36,430
Here you go.

72
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:38,850
I'll hang your towel here.

73
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:42,410
I've never done this for anyone before.

74
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:44,270
I only do it for you.

75
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:06,040
(Yin as Theartha)

76
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:13,710
(War as Mungkorn)

77
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:20,200
(Shane as Phuwin)

78
00:05:20,630 --> 00:05:23,670
(Boss as Lukplub)

79
00:05:26,050 --> 00:05:27,780
(Kit as Kanin)

80
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,990
(Tang as Nadol)

81
00:05:33,470 --> 00:05:38,710
(Tae as Saming)

82
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:10,200
I don't see even a single shrimp, Khaopuk?

83
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,770
Did you see Lady Pharada
eating shrimp?

84
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,700
She has shrimp porridge every day.

85
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:15,610
Good morning.

86
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:17,450
- Good morning.
- Good morning, Mr. Mungkorn.

87
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,510
Omelet and fresh veggies look so good.

88
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,090
I'll just sit and eat with you guys.

89
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,060
- Oops.
- You can't.

90
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:23,440
Absolutely not, Mr. Mungkorn.

91
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:24,700
You can't sit here.

92
00:06:24,730 --> 00:06:26,700
You have to sit at the table outside.

93
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,250
You're the Inspector's wife now.

94
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,590
You can't eat in the kitchen.

95
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:31,620
Go eat at the table outside.

96
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,940
- Khaomao, you need to update.
- About what?

97
00:06:34,150 --> 00:06:35,790
We shouldn't specify positions.

98
00:06:35,950 --> 00:06:36,900
What positions are you talking about?

99
00:06:37,210 --> 00:06:39,580
You'd better call them
husband and husband.

100
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:41,020
Oh.

101
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:42,870
Mr. Mungkorn is the son-in-law of this house.

102
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:45,430
So you're like our boss now.

103
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:47,300
It's best to eat over there.

104
00:06:47,830 --> 00:06:49,130
Please don't think of me like that.

105
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:51,260
Just consider me as your family.

106
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:53,160
No, no, no.

107
00:06:53,190 --> 00:06:55,750
Now that you've been given
this opportunity,

108
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:59,460
you must learn to be bossy
and arrogant.

109
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:01,470
Go full-on dramatic.

110
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:05,050
You can call us servants if you like,

111
00:07:05,070 --> 00:07:06,810
but please don't go so far
as to call us bitches.

112
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,950
Mr. Mungkorn, you'd better go wait
at the table.

113
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:11,630
Here is for maids like us.

114
00:07:11,710 --> 00:07:12,590
That way, please.

115
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:14,210
Alright.

116
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,390
Actually, this way
we don't have to share food.

117
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:21,090
We already don't have enough as it is.

118
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,560
Exactly, this is all we've got.

119
00:07:23,670 --> 00:07:26,340
Mungkorn, tell us what you want.

120
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,440
Khaomao and Khaopuk can cook anything.

121
00:07:29,430 --> 00:07:31,570
Please don't order anything too difficult.

122
00:07:31,590 --> 00:07:33,460
We didn't graduate from Le Cordon Bleu.

123
00:07:33,850 --> 00:07:35,810
We're better at making bar snacks.

124
00:07:35,970 --> 00:07:38,400
Laab or luu can do those.

125
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:39,940
Honestly, anything is fine.

126
00:07:39,970 --> 00:07:41,230
I'm not that picky.

127
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:44,000
Good morning, honey.

128
00:07:49,370 --> 00:07:53,040
I guess we should just
throw away this dessert.

129
00:07:53,070 --> 00:07:54,790
It can't compare to how sweet they are.

130
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:55,950
Well...

131
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:59,780
I wish I had a morning kiss like that.

132
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,950
Want me to give you a kiss?

133
00:08:04,810 --> 00:08:06,420
Stop joking around.

134
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,660
You should eat.

135
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,150
Have some of this, Mungkorn.

136
00:08:11,330 --> 00:08:12,170
Let me feed you.

137
00:08:12,310 --> 00:08:14,570
No need. I can eat by myself.

138
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,950
Go on, eat, Mungkorn.

139
00:08:15,970 --> 00:08:17,530
Thear is going out of his way
to feed you, dear.

140
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:23,730
My Lady.

141
00:08:24,470 --> 00:08:26,910
Their relationship is moving
faster than the Shinkansen.

142
00:08:26,990 --> 00:08:27,970
They fell in love all on their own.

143
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,080
I haven't even done anything yet.

144
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:32,490
Just a second.

145
00:08:41,530 --> 00:08:42,850
Is it good?

146
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:44,760
It's delicious.

147
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:50,070
Hey, Inspector.
Are you okay?

148
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:52,430
Or do you need some kind of help?

149
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,440
I'm perfectly fine.

150
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:58,550
Breakfast is so important.

151
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,610
You'll feel energized
and ready for the day.

152
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,170
But I think this is a bit weird.

153
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:08,480
Just don't question anything.

154
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:10,510
Let me take care of you.

155
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,870
This is what I do best.

156
00:09:16,410 --> 00:09:19,650
So, let's move your things in today

157
00:09:20,170 --> 00:09:20,890
What?

158
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:23,920
Don't I have to move to the
police flats in Chiang Mai?

159
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,650
That's even better.

160
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:27,640
This house is way more comfortable.

161
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:29,310
Why go live in a cramped flat?

162
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:31,250
And I think...

163
00:09:31,330 --> 00:09:32,450
you should stay here,

164
00:09:32,470 --> 00:09:35,480
so I can see you two being lovebirds.

165
00:09:35,830 --> 00:09:36,940
Right, Thear?

166
00:09:37,090 --> 00:09:38,370
That's right, Mom.

167
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:42,250
I'll feed you shrimp every day.

168
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,060
Lady Pharada, may I have some shrimp?

169
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:55,340
After you, Mungkorn.

170
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:00,840
Hold on.

171
00:10:04,410 --> 00:10:05,790
I can't let this slide.

172
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:11,070
Why didn't you tie your shoes properly?

173
00:10:11,370 --> 00:10:13,420
If you ever trip and fall,

174
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:15,390
I'm gonna feel the pain right here.

175
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:18,480
All done.

176
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,480
Step back a bit.

177
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:23,060
Let me get the door for you.

178
00:10:24,310 --> 00:10:25,140
Please, get in.

179
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:26,860
Wait a second.

180
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,430
This is a neck pillow.

181
00:10:32,530 --> 00:10:33,940
You'll be in the car for a long time.

182
00:10:33,990 --> 00:10:35,850
I'm worried you'll get stiff.

183
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:38,170
Here.

184
00:10:38,590 --> 00:10:39,680
Mungkorn, get in, please.

185
00:10:39,770 --> 00:10:41,440
Watch your head.
I don't want you to get hurt.

186
00:10:41,470 --> 00:10:42,310
Get in slowly.

187
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:43,730
Okay, be careful.

188
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,210
See you, Mom.

189
00:10:48,910 --> 00:10:51,160
So this is how beautiful love can be.

190
00:10:53,930 --> 00:10:54,970
Look, Cupid.

191
00:10:54,990 --> 00:10:56,940
How cute this couple is

192
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:59,920
I want to wake up to see this every day.

193
00:11:00,530 --> 00:11:01,240
You're right.

194
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:02,970
It's exactly like you said, My Lady.

195
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,520
Just get married first,
and you can work on the relationship later.

196
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:08,500
Love really is all about fate.

197
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,760
You're gonna wreck the brakes.

198
00:11:27,750 --> 00:11:29,860
You're such a great actor.

199
00:11:30,050 --> 00:11:31,930
I should nominate you
for a Nataraja Award.

200
00:11:31,970 --> 00:11:33,560
If you weren't putting on that act,

201
00:11:33,910 --> 00:11:35,210
I couldn't handle my mom.

202
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,500
What do you mean?

203
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:38,260
Come on, like this morning.

204
00:11:39,130 --> 00:11:40,840
We've already slept in the same room.

205
00:11:40,930 --> 00:11:42,490
What more could we possibly have to do?

206
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,570
Thear, listen.

207
00:11:43,930 --> 00:11:46,830
When I had you get married,
it wasn't just for the title.

208
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:50,800
You need to have that
real couple energy.

209
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:53,320
That's why I had Mungkorn
marry into our family.

210
00:11:53,990 --> 00:11:57,540
I've already done everything
the oracle told us to do.

211
00:11:57,910 --> 00:12:00,680
I want you to treat him like your partner.

212
00:12:00,850 --> 00:12:03,220
Do you think getting married
is going to fix everything?

213
00:12:03,610 --> 00:12:05,210
Heaven and earth are watching over us.

214
00:12:05,230 --> 00:12:07,570
I'm sure they can sense the truth.

215
00:12:08,070 --> 00:12:09,110
Trust me.

216
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:12,290
It's just a fake marriage,

217
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:15,340
so how can I get that 'couple energy'
you keep talking about?

218
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:17,200
If you don't have it, just make it up.

219
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:21,710
Start by being nice to each other.

220
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:25,220
Do cute little things for each other,
day by day.

221
00:12:25,330 --> 00:12:27,160
He'll be your true love one day.

222
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,930
Are you through menopause?
You're so pushy.

223
00:12:30,930 --> 00:12:31,730
You have to do it.

224
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:35,900
Fine, I'll take care of it.

225
00:12:36,110 --> 00:12:36,760
Right.

226
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:40,610
You understand
the whole situation now, right?

227
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:41,810
That means...

228
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:44,350
We'll only act like lovey-dovey husbands

229
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:45,510
at home.

230
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,110
Once we're outside,

231
00:12:47,270 --> 00:12:49,180
we're just boss and subordinate.

232
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:51,840
And don't tell anyone about this.

233
00:12:52,330 --> 00:12:54,290
Or else my 'Cunning Inspector' image
takes a hit.

234
00:12:54,490 --> 00:12:55,130
Got it?

235
00:12:55,630 --> 00:12:56,440
I understand.

236
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:58,810
Hey.

237
00:12:58,990 --> 00:13:00,130
You're disappointed, aren't you?

238
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,150
Everyone would die to be my partner.

239
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:07,730
Are you full?

240
00:13:08,610 --> 00:13:09,400
What?

241
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:10,710
Are you full of yourself?

242
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:12,750
How full of yourself are you?

243
00:13:13,010 --> 00:13:14,910
I don't want anyone
to know about this, either.

244
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:19,870
That's perfect then.

245
00:13:20,540 --> 00:13:21,650
I want my pillow back.

246
00:13:22,990 --> 00:13:24,340
I bought it for myself.

247
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:31,100
Let's go.

248
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,380
(Chiang Rai Provincial Police Flats)

249
00:13:45,970 --> 00:13:47,120
Wait, wait, wait.

250
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:50,240
You're just moving out,
not going on patrol.

251
00:13:50,270 --> 00:13:52,630
You don't need to take
a map of Thailand with you.

252
00:13:52,670 --> 00:13:53,250
Oh.

253
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:55,170
Why am I taking this?

254
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:56,940
My bad.

255
00:13:57,860 --> 00:13:59,270
I've just got a lot on my mind.

256
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:03,140
Don't you want to move out?

257
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:04,290
Of course I do.

258
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:06,490
It's just...

259
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:09,090
I don't know. I'm feeling a bit conflicted.

260
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,040
Trust me.

261
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:11,500
It's better for you to be there.

262
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:13,840
You'll get to enjoy the city life
in Chiang Mai.

263
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:15,320
The restaurants there stay open late.

264
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:17,080
I know you love your late-night snacks.

265
00:14:17,970 --> 00:14:21,420
It's not just about food.

266
00:14:21,810 --> 00:14:23,610
There are things I have to think about.

267
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:27,200
Just think about it.

268
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:30,300
You're moving to work on a major case.

269
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:31,500
That's awesome.

270
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:33,120
Why are you hesitating?

271
00:14:33,530 --> 00:14:36,610
If you don't take it now,
who knows when you'll get another chance?

272
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:41,210
Hey.

273
00:14:42,270 --> 00:14:43,830
Oh.

274
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:45,720
Is this a photo of you as a kid?

275
00:14:46,490 --> 00:14:47,620
That was over ten years ago.

276
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:49,760
- This was me as a kid.
- You look like a Korean idol.

277
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:53,380
You're not done yet?

278
00:14:53,470 --> 00:14:54,400
Why is it taking so long?

279
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:58,110
Because Mungkorn has so much stuff.

280
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:00,310
If you're not gonna help,
then stop complaining.

281
00:15:00,450 --> 00:15:01,930
I'm not complaining.

282
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,530
I was just asking because
I'm worried about you.

283
00:15:08,770 --> 00:15:09,600
Are you tired?

284
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,170
Yeah, I'm exhausted.

285
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:12,500
Give me some support.

286
00:15:18,030 --> 00:15:20,430
Did you forget I'm right here?

287
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:24,740
Hey, buddy.

288
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:27,710
I could use some support too.

289
00:15:27,830 --> 00:15:29,330
Nobody's giving any to me.

290
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:30,330
Well...

291
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:33,350
If you want one,
go find your own sweetheart.

292
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:36,990
You want me to find a sweetheart?

293
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:40,190
Sarge, help me find one.

294
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:41,200
Oh.

295
00:15:41,250 --> 00:15:42,850
You've got plenty of girls lined up.

296
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:44,580
Just pick one.

297
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:47,860
Are you done packing?

298
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,650
No one's gonna mind
if you take more stuff.

299
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:51,110
Don't exaggerate.

300
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:53,770
I'm only staying there for six months.
Why am I taking so much stuff?

301
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:54,980
Hey, just in case.

302
00:15:55,390 --> 00:15:57,520
What if it lasts longer than six months?

303
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,170
No way.

304
00:15:59,510 --> 00:16:01,030
Six months is enough.

305
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,140
No more, no less.

306
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:15,540
See you later.

307
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:16,600
It won't be long.

308
00:16:18,830 --> 00:16:20,350
Take good care of Mungkorn.

309
00:16:20,670 --> 00:16:22,090
Don't let any bad guys hit on him.

310
00:16:22,190 --> 00:16:23,660
Don't let him get hurt.

311
00:16:23,970 --> 00:16:26,130
And don't let anyone make him cry.

312
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:29,170
Oh, yes, sir.

313
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:31,220
I'll take care of your little brother

314
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,270
better than anyone ever could, buddy.

315
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:34,810
That's not necessary.

316
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:37,650
Let him spend his time
taking care of his girls.

317
00:16:38,490 --> 00:16:39,350
I can't do that.

318
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:41,280
Since my best friend entrusted me,

319
00:16:41,610 --> 00:16:43,010
I have to take excellent care of you.

320
00:16:46,730 --> 00:16:47,920
- See ya.
- See ya.

321
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,670
See? I even opened the door for him.

322
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:51,590
Please, get in.

323
00:16:54,870 --> 00:16:56,070
I'll take great care of him, buddy.

324
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:57,210
Yeah.

325
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,700
- See ya, bud.
- See ya.

326
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:00,610
- See you, Lukplub.
- See you.

327
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:14,710
As for you...

328
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:16,790
I'm going to take very good care of you.

329
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:17,840
Let's go back to our room.

330
00:17:35,170 --> 00:17:37,690
Whoa, bear-print pajamas?

331
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:38,980
Are you trying to be all cute?

332
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:41,140
Why?

333
00:17:41,910 --> 00:17:44,050
Can't a cop like cute things?

334
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,740
I'm not saying anything.
It actually suits you.

335
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:49,940
Just pick out whatever you want.

336
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:51,460
I'll pay for it.

337
00:17:51,730 --> 00:17:53,350
Think of it as part of our deal.

338
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:55,510
Being the Inspector's partner,
you have to look good.

339
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:00,260
How good do I have to look?

340
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:02,520
I can't pull off that fancy look.

341
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:06,000
Like I could ever be worthy of you.

342
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,480
Since you're so high and mighty.

343
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,240
You don't need to dress up much.

344
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,080
Let me take a look.

345
00:18:12,630 --> 00:18:15,230
You're good-looking enough.

346
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,760
Even if your birth matched
what the oracle said,

347
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,010
I wouldn't have married you

348
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:22,630
if you weren't cute enough.

349
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:25,460
We have to live together for six months.

350
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:27,850
So I need something cute to look at.

351
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:29,600
This one will do.

352
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:34,830
I see.

353
00:18:36,330 --> 00:18:38,060
So you only date people for their looks?

354
00:18:38,710 --> 00:18:41,660
If they're no longer good-looking,
you'll just leave them, right?

355
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:43,760
No wonder.

356
00:18:44,310 --> 00:18:45,390
No wonder what?

357
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:48,460
No wonder you haven't been
able to settle down with anyone.

358
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:54,120
Well, why don't you try?

359
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:56,900
That's not my job.

360
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,750
My job is to put an end to the bad luck.

361
00:19:00,110 --> 00:19:01,310
Not to get you settled down.

362
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:05,420
I don't think anyone
could ever get you to settle down

363
00:19:06,330 --> 00:19:07,730
unless you choose to.

364
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,800
'Cause nobody's given me
a reason to settle down yet.

365
00:19:13,950 --> 00:19:16,030
Excuse me, is there a fitting room?

366
00:19:16,130 --> 00:19:18,200
Yes, the fitting room is over there.

367
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:18,850
Sh*t.

368
00:19:18,870 --> 00:19:19,870
- Hey, Mungkorn.
- What the hell?

369
00:19:19,890 --> 00:19:20,830
- Yeah, just go first.
- Inspector.

370
00:19:21,350 --> 00:19:22,590
- What?
- Just go in.

371
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:25,780
They're pretty, right? Both of them.

372
00:19:25,810 --> 00:19:27,160
I'm just picking out clothes.

373
00:19:30,580 --> 00:19:31,380
What?

374
00:19:32,570 --> 00:19:34,120
That woman who just walked in.

375
00:19:35,350 --> 00:19:36,100
She's my ex-fling.

376
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:38,130
She really wants me to be her boyfriend,

377
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:38,870
but I'm not interested.

378
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:40,360
Then tell her you're not interested.

379
00:19:40,390 --> 00:19:41,950
I already told her,
but she didn't listen.

380
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:44,590
She thinks I'm single,
so she still has a chance.

381
00:19:44,610 --> 00:19:46,580
You probably gave her a chance.

382
00:19:46,910 --> 00:19:47,900
Serves you right.

383
00:19:47,930 --> 00:19:49,320
Now you're scolding me?

384
00:19:49,670 --> 00:19:51,350
Well, I'm a handsome guy.
What can I do?

385
00:19:53,630 --> 00:19:54,720
Hey, kids.

386
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,710
What are you two doing in there?

387
00:19:58,420 --> 00:19:59,980
- I'm gonna tell her...
- Come out right now.

388
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:01,750
- Stay here.
- My customer needs the room.

389
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,670
This is a clothing store, not a motel.

390
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:07,590
Just a second, dear.

391
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:09,790
People these days have no shame.

392
00:20:09,810 --> 00:20:11,040
They get turned on anywhere.

393
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:11,960
Oh.

394
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:14,600
Can't they just wait and do it at home?

395
00:20:15,770 --> 00:20:16,570
Take my shirt off.

396
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,360
- Help me. Pull the shirt up.
- What?

397
00:20:18,530 --> 00:20:19,860
You're not coming out, are you?

398
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:23,800
Take it off. Hurry.

399
00:20:24,590 --> 00:20:26,050
I'm going to open it myself.

400
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:29,310
He was just trying on a shirt.

401
00:20:29,330 --> 00:20:30,800
His shirt got stuck
while he was taking it off.

402
00:20:31,690 --> 00:20:32,520
Then why didn't you say so?

403
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:33,780
- Let me help.
- That's okay.

404
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:35,380
My friend is an introvert.

405
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,830
He doesn't like being touched.

406
00:20:37,390 --> 00:20:38,340
Please, go ahead and use the room.

407
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:40,590
- We'll go take it off outside instead.
- Wait.

408
00:20:40,810 --> 00:20:42,740
What about those bear-print pajamas

409
00:20:42,770 --> 00:20:44,780
you were looking for earlier?
Don't you want them?

410
00:20:45,650 --> 00:20:46,460
I do.

411
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,130
- I'll take them.
- Hold on.

412
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,780
Here they are.

413
00:20:54,810 --> 00:20:56,060
- Let's go.
- Wait, wait for the change.

414
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:56,810
Keep the change.

415
00:20:56,970 --> 00:20:57,920
Consider it a fee for the hangers.

416
00:20:58,290 --> 00:20:59,050
Thank you, dear.

417
00:20:59,220 --> 00:21:00,060
You're so kind.

418
00:21:04,530 --> 00:21:05,190
That's enough.

419
00:21:05,610 --> 00:21:06,700
- Is she gone?
- Yeah, she's gone.

420
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,260
We almost got caught.

421
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:10,550
I'm out of ideas to get away from her.

422
00:21:11,730 --> 00:21:14,310
How many more of your girls
am I going to have to deal with?

423
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:15,160
Whoa.

424
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:16,120
A lot.

425
00:21:16,280 --> 00:21:17,280
Too many to count.

426
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:22,580
I won't help you next time.
You're on your own.

427
00:21:23,150 --> 00:21:23,620
Hey.

428
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:27,280
Thank God.

429
00:21:33,950 --> 00:21:35,210
Wow.

430
00:21:35,570 --> 00:21:37,090
Bear-print pajamas.

431
00:21:37,650 --> 00:21:40,990
You look cute, sexy,
and adorable, honey.

432
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:44,410
Are there cameras in the room too?

433
00:21:44,590 --> 00:21:45,630
Why do we have to put on an act?

434
00:21:45,830 --> 00:21:46,990
There aren't any cameras.

435
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:48,840
But my mom said

436
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:51,180
we need to have that couple energy.

437
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:52,610
Come on.

438
00:21:54,510 --> 00:21:55,470
Time for bed. Come here.

439
00:22:08,820 --> 00:22:10,230
Are we gonna sleep like this?

440
00:22:22,630 --> 00:22:23,900
Are you a bit too close?

441
00:22:24,350 --> 00:22:25,090
Hey.

442
00:22:26,210 --> 00:22:27,790
Even if my mom isn't watching,

443
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:30,980
but this house has guardian spirits.

444
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:32,700
They might be watching us.

445
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:48,900
Think of it as practice,

446
00:22:49,600 --> 00:22:51,480
in case we have to put on an act
every morning.

447
00:22:51,590 --> 00:22:52,840
My mom might come check on us.

448
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:08,980
You squinted like this.

449
00:23:10,730 --> 00:23:11,900
You're so tense.

450
00:23:12,020 --> 00:23:13,210
Are you getting a bit too serious?

451
00:23:13,530 --> 00:23:14,660
I was just going to say goodnight.

452
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:16,190
Goodnight.

453
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:18,090
You were like this.

454
00:23:22,740 --> 00:23:24,390
You were quite sexy, actually.

455
00:23:34,330 --> 00:23:35,260
Goodnight.

456
00:24:01,510 --> 00:24:03,340
Inspector, time to wake up.

457
00:24:06,500 --> 00:24:08,650
No, I want to sleep longer.

458
00:24:08,690 --> 00:24:09,960
Stop bothering me.

459
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:15,100
Honey, wake up. It's time for work.

460
00:24:17,960 --> 00:24:20,330
Stop bothering me.

461
00:24:20,770 --> 00:24:22,130
You don't have to go this far.

462
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,360
My mom isn't going to come in.

463
00:24:24,910 --> 00:24:25,910
I'm not playing around.

464
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:29,600
I really want to wake you up, honey.

465
00:24:32,210 --> 00:24:33,120
Hey.

466
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:35,030
What are you trying to do?

467
00:24:35,810 --> 00:24:37,490
Well, you just wouldn't wake up.

468
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:40,120
So I'll have to try something new.

469
00:24:43,590 --> 00:24:44,880
I don't think that's a good idea.

470
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:51,240
Oh.

471
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:53,240
Are you waking up now?

472
00:24:55,340 --> 00:24:56,600
Yeah, something is.

473
00:24:58,480 --> 00:24:59,150
Hey.

474
00:25:05,310 --> 00:25:06,820
Are you awake yet?

475
00:25:08,580 --> 00:25:09,890
I'm fully awake now.

476
00:25:11,810 --> 00:25:13,250
Now that you're awake...

477
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:14,870
you should get out of bed.

478
00:25:15,410 --> 00:25:16,410
You're going to be late.

479
00:25:16,590 --> 00:25:17,510
I'm off.

480
00:25:19,790 --> 00:25:21,280
Go take a shower, quickly, Inspector.

481
00:25:24,330 --> 00:25:26,390
You must take responsibility for this.

482
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:28,900
You can't just wake 'Big Thear' up and leave.

483
00:25:31,170 --> 00:25:32,100
Fine.

484
00:25:33,770 --> 00:25:36,180
You dare mess with Big Thear?

485
00:25:42,580 --> 00:25:45,970
I'm going to introduce you
to my talented team.

486
00:25:47,030 --> 00:25:49,710
We take great pride in this team

487
00:25:49,940 --> 00:25:51,540
I guarantee you'll be impressed.

488
00:25:51,660 --> 00:25:52,780
I'm thrilled.

489
00:25:53,930 --> 00:25:54,550
Come on.

490
00:25:54,940 --> 00:25:55,910
Yes, Inspector.

491
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:57,680
It's mine!

492
00:25:58,170 --> 00:25:59,940
It belongs to the government,
not to you.

493
00:26:00,110 --> 00:26:00,740
I'm going to sit here.

494
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:02,360
I'm sitting here too. Get up.

495
00:26:03,140 --> 00:26:04,410
I'm not getting up. I'm sitting.

496
00:26:04,550 --> 00:26:05,160
Get up.

497
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:06,460
Are you going to get up or not?

498
00:26:06,900 --> 00:26:08,390
- I'm not.
- Get up!

499
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:10,390
- I'm not.
- Fine, then I'll sit too.

500
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:11,330
What are you doing, Captain?

501
00:26:11,490 --> 00:26:12,800
Captain!

502
00:26:12,840 --> 00:26:14,210
- Get up.
- No.

503
00:26:14,230 --> 00:26:15,830
- Stand up.
- No way.

504
00:26:16,090 --> 00:26:17,970
- I told you to get up.
- I said no.

505
00:26:18,320 --> 00:26:19,360
- Captain!
- No.

506
00:26:19,620 --> 00:26:21,280
- Captain, get up.
- No.

507
00:26:21,310 --> 00:26:22,710
- Get up!
- No.

508
00:26:22,730 --> 00:26:23,660
Aren't you gonna get up?

509
00:26:25,450 --> 00:26:26,050
Hey!

510
00:26:33,220 --> 00:26:34,480
You guys.

511
00:26:35,270 --> 00:26:36,850
Aren't you embarrassed
in front of the new kid?

512
00:26:38,580 --> 00:26:39,510
Sergeant Mungkorn.

513
00:26:39,700 --> 00:26:41,160
Everyone, this is Sergeant Mungkorn.

514
00:26:42,370 --> 00:26:43,620
Let me introduce them to you.

515
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:47,640
On my left here is

516
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:49,400
Police Captain Kanin.

517
00:26:49,570 --> 00:26:51,260
He transferred from Chiang Rai Station,

518
00:26:51,430 --> 00:26:53,530
specifically to handle the Black Bull case.

519
00:26:53,550 --> 00:26:54,910
And on my right

520
00:26:55,060 --> 00:26:56,250
is Police Captain Nadol.

521
00:26:56,290 --> 00:26:58,180
They call him the 'Ice Sculpture.'

522
00:26:58,430 --> 00:27:00,340
Handsome, cold, and cool.

523
00:27:00,470 --> 00:27:02,050
He looks quiet, but he's razor-sharp.

524
00:27:02,200 --> 00:27:03,910
He's an expert in strategy and IT.

525
00:27:04,110 --> 00:27:06,450
Hello. Welcome to the team.

526
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:07,980
Feel free to ask me anything.

527
00:27:08,300 --> 00:27:09,040
Yes, sir.

528
00:27:09,470 --> 00:27:10,570
Don't bother asking this guy.

529
00:27:10,740 --> 00:27:11,810
He's not much of a help.

530
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,210
You'd better ask Nadol.

531
00:27:13,350 --> 00:27:15,120
He's basically the station's AI.

532
00:27:15,670 --> 00:27:17,160
And besides being an AI,

533
00:27:17,260 --> 00:27:19,660
he's also the station's smart-ass.

534
00:27:20,520 --> 00:27:22,700
I'm a smart-ass to those who deserve it.

535
00:27:22,720 --> 00:27:23,900
So why are you being one to me?

536
00:27:24,620 --> 00:27:27,420
I deserve to be loved.

537
00:27:27,850 --> 00:27:30,520
No one could ever love
someone like you.

538
00:27:34,700 --> 00:27:35,990
With all this bickering,

539
00:27:36,110 --> 00:27:37,290
you two might actually fall in love.

540
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:38,330
- No way.
- Not a chance.

541
00:27:40,050 --> 00:27:40,850
What great teamwork.

542
00:27:41,770 --> 00:27:44,180
He is Sergeant Maruay.

543
00:27:45,060 --> 00:27:45,860
Hello.

544
00:27:46,140 --> 00:27:46,930
Hello.

545
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:48,150
And this is Lieutenant Mai.

546
00:27:48,260 --> 00:27:49,030
Hello.

547
00:27:50,040 --> 00:27:50,970
Inspector...

548
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:56,200
Can these two really work together?

549
00:28:03,700 --> 00:28:04,460
Don't worry.

550
00:28:05,110 --> 00:28:07,060
My team is nothing but the best.

551
00:28:08,760 --> 00:28:09,560
I am

552
00:28:09,830 --> 00:28:12,940
Police Sergeant Major
Makwaen Luelandong,

553
00:28:13,130 --> 00:28:14,310
the Femme Fatale Informant.

554
00:28:14,360 --> 00:28:17,590
Men, women, or LGBTQIA+ people,

555
00:28:17,720 --> 00:28:19,040
whether they're secretly having affairs

556
00:28:19,090 --> 00:28:20,360
or being someone's side chick,

557
00:28:20,500 --> 00:28:23,060
nothing escapes my eyes.

558
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:26,280
Who's perfect, who's a mess,
or what their sexual orientation is,

559
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:27,600
I know it all.

560
00:28:28,470 --> 00:28:29,820
That's some very detailed info.

561
00:28:30,780 --> 00:28:31,450
Makwaen.

562
00:28:32,260 --> 00:28:33,400
This is Sergeant Mungkorn.

563
00:28:33,490 --> 00:28:35,800
He transferred from Chiang Rai
to join our team.

564
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:39,110
Hello.
I'm Sergeant Mungkorn Phianwanich.

565
00:28:39,220 --> 00:28:41,860
A good cop, ready to tackle any case.

566
00:28:41,990 --> 00:28:44,000
Alright, for your first mission,

567
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:46,230
I'm giving you a huge responsibility,

568
00:28:47,190 --> 00:28:49,050
one that nobody else ever wants.

569
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:50,400
You got it, Inspector.

570
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:51,130
Are you ready?

571
00:28:51,310 --> 00:28:51,840
Ready.

572
00:28:51,860 --> 00:28:52,780
Is that the best you can do?

573
00:28:52,860 --> 00:28:53,460
I'm ready, sir.

574
00:28:53,490 --> 00:28:54,420
Okay.

575
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:56,290
Here.

576
00:28:57,060 --> 00:28:58,100
What case is it, Inspector?

577
00:28:58,330 --> 00:29:00,480
Sort these documents
according to the timeline for me.

578
00:29:00,730 --> 00:29:03,030
Everyone else is just too busy.

579
00:29:03,270 --> 00:29:05,210
Makwaen, keep an eye on him.

580
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:07,000
Good luck, Sarge.

581
00:29:07,340 --> 00:29:08,040
I'm counting on you.

582
00:29:15,630 --> 00:29:16,630
He's so intense.

583
00:29:16,650 --> 00:29:18,550
You have to be like that
in front of him.

584
00:29:20,380 --> 00:29:21,900
- Hey, Sarge, you won't believe this.
- Yes?

585
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:23,810
These are all the documents.

586
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:26,010
I've been sorting these by myself
for nearly two months.

587
00:29:26,040 --> 00:29:27,060
I'm still not finished.

588
00:29:27,080 --> 00:29:28,590
- Two whole months?
- Yeah.

589
00:29:28,710 --> 00:29:30,840
I sort this pile,
and then a new pile shows up.

590
00:29:30,980 --> 00:29:32,950
I sort that pile,
and another one appears.

591
00:29:33,140 --> 00:29:35,160
We can't get any real work done.

592
00:29:35,280 --> 00:29:37,070
So, where should I start?

593
00:29:37,100 --> 00:29:39,510
Well, right here.
They need to be sorted by date,

594
00:29:39,540 --> 00:29:41,060
and then by the numbers here.

595
00:29:41,130 --> 00:29:42,110
- Okay.
- Like this.

596
00:29:42,150 --> 00:29:43,780
It's a relief having you to help me.

597
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:45,250
Yeah, let's tackle this together.

598
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:47,110
- Oh, Sarge?
- Yes?

599
00:29:47,140 --> 00:29:48,440
I just remembered...

600
00:29:48,940 --> 00:29:51,230
I ordered some corn dogs
and spicy glass noodle salad.

601
00:29:51,500 --> 00:29:53,170
Can I go grab them for a moment?

602
00:29:53,250 --> 00:29:54,570
- You won't be long, right?
- About a month.

603
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:56,180
Oh, a month, right?
Wait, what?

604
00:29:56,660 --> 00:29:57,860
Just kidding.

605
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:59,840
I'll be right back. Just a second,
it's over here.

606
00:30:02,020 --> 00:30:03,290
Was she joking or serious?

607
00:30:25,980 --> 00:30:26,670
Mungkorn.

608
00:30:27,300 --> 00:30:27,850
Yes, sir.

609
00:30:27,870 --> 00:30:29,610
Go get me some coffee.
I want a dark roast.

610
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:30,440
Excuse me...

611
00:30:31,050 --> 00:30:33,390
I'd like six black coffees.
Three sweetened and three unsweetened.

612
00:30:33,520 --> 00:30:34,090
Got it.

613
00:30:40,180 --> 00:30:41,560
Here's your coffee. No charge.

614
00:30:41,810 --> 00:30:42,440
Thank you.

615
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:46,630
Sarge, refill the printer ink cartridge.

616
00:31:11,230 --> 00:31:12,000
Hello.

617
00:31:16,340 --> 00:31:17,000
Sarge.

618
00:31:20,010 --> 00:31:21,240
Write a summary for this case.

619
00:31:22,070 --> 00:31:22,920
Inspector...

620
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:24,700
It's been weeks already.

621
00:31:25,130 --> 00:31:26,220
Where's that major case you promised me?

622
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:28,240
Mopping floors and running errands?

623
00:31:28,670 --> 00:31:29,630
Getting coffee?

624
00:31:29,780 --> 00:31:31,150
Refilling printer ink?

625
00:31:31,330 --> 00:31:33,020
I can do much more than this.

626
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:35,580
Yeah, I know you're dedicated.

627
00:31:36,030 --> 00:31:39,200
But someone like you
still has a lot to prove.

628
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:42,270
Tell me what I have to do.

629
00:31:42,700 --> 00:31:43,830
I'm ready to prove myself.

630
00:31:45,250 --> 00:31:46,160
Here's the thing.

631
00:31:46,710 --> 00:31:48,120
You're just way too soft.

632
00:31:48,700 --> 00:31:50,960
Remember that case when
Ronnaphop had a seizure?

633
00:31:51,390 --> 00:31:53,290
It was a total mess.

634
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:56,050
I can be tougher if I have to.

635
00:31:56,230 --> 00:31:57,150
Really?

636
00:31:58,410 --> 00:31:59,780
With a cute face like yours?

637
00:32:01,220 --> 00:32:03,490
Go on, then. Do it if you can.

638
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:04,890
Give me your best tough-guy look.

639
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:07,410
If you don't,
I'm not taking you on the mission.

640
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:08,860
Come on. Do it.

641
00:32:10,550 --> 00:32:12,320
You need to look even tougher.

642
00:32:13,320 --> 00:32:15,240
We need to scare those criminals.

643
00:32:18,330 --> 00:32:19,810
Tougher! Come on, give me more.

644
00:32:20,630 --> 00:32:21,270
More!

645
00:32:22,320 --> 00:32:24,910
Come on, Mungkorn.
Live up to your name.

646
00:32:24,960 --> 00:32:26,660
Be more intimidating.

647
00:32:30,390 --> 00:32:31,230
Here comes Mungkorn.

648
00:32:32,040 --> 00:32:32,710
That's it.

649
00:32:33,390 --> 00:32:34,230
More!

650
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,680
Now breathe fire.

651
00:32:37,700 --> 00:32:38,730
Breathe that fire, Mungkorn.

652
00:32:48,280 --> 00:32:49,450
Stop playing around, Inspector.

653
00:32:49,810 --> 00:32:51,840
If I were a criminal,
I'd be peeing my pants right now.

654
00:32:51,990 --> 00:32:53,110
I'm here to remind you about the promise.

655
00:32:53,960 --> 00:32:55,490
You said once we got married,

656
00:32:55,790 --> 00:32:57,010
you'd let me handle the major cases.

657
00:32:57,140 --> 00:32:57,870
So, where are they?

658
00:32:58,990 --> 00:32:59,590
Show me.

659
00:33:00,190 --> 00:33:02,510
What if I break that promise?

660
00:33:03,360 --> 00:33:04,070
What are you going to do?

661
00:33:06,060 --> 00:33:07,220
Oh...

662
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:10,290
Will you tell everyone...

663
00:33:11,410 --> 00:33:12,550
that I'm your husband?

664
00:33:13,230 --> 00:33:14,600
You think that I won't dare to do it?

665
00:33:15,530 --> 00:33:16,990
Because if I actually do it,

666
00:33:18,050 --> 00:33:20,940
all your girls will go away.

667
00:33:21,910 --> 00:33:23,400
- Whoa!
- You want them to find out?

668
00:33:23,730 --> 00:33:25,050
Are you threatening me?

669
00:33:25,380 --> 00:33:26,370
You're a fast learner,
I'll give you that.

670
00:33:27,070 --> 00:33:28,520
Go ahead. Do it.

671
00:33:29,080 --> 00:33:30,570
You're dying to do it anyway, right?

672
00:33:30,790 --> 00:33:32,360
You wanna tell the world

673
00:33:32,370 --> 00:33:32,800
that you're my...

674
00:33:32,800 --> 00:33:34,240
Inspector Thear and I are...

675
00:33:35,490 --> 00:33:36,480
Hus...

676
00:33:46,450 --> 00:33:48,060
I know now that you will actually do it.

677
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:50,530
I won't break my promise.

678
00:33:51,720 --> 00:33:52,800
But just be patient.

679
00:33:54,190 --> 00:33:56,170
I'll give you a chance
to show what you've got soon.

680
00:33:56,440 --> 00:33:57,030
Okay?

681
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:01,030
Just don't chicken out
when the time has come.

682
00:34:02,780 --> 00:34:03,690
I won't.

683
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:06,820
But remember this,

684
00:34:07,420 --> 00:34:11,550
I remember everything you've said.

685
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:14,510
I'm going to grab some lunch.

686
00:34:18,960 --> 00:34:20,380
Order some khao soi for me too.

687
00:34:21,300 --> 00:34:23,090
Extra chicken drumsticks, please.

688
00:34:34,820 --> 00:34:35,930
Mungkorn.

689
00:34:36,750 --> 00:34:38,100
Since you started working here

690
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:39,830
our jobs have become so much easier.

691
00:34:40,510 --> 00:34:41,970
The documents you have sorted

692
00:34:42,310 --> 00:34:44,320
are so easy to find and read now.

693
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:45,770
Thank you so much.

694
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:46,700
Really?

695
00:34:48,560 --> 00:34:50,790
I'm so happy that
I could be of help to everyone.

696
00:34:54,550 --> 00:34:55,960
Thear.

697
00:34:56,630 --> 00:34:57,630
I missed you so much.

698
00:34:57,650 --> 00:34:59,640
Where have you been?
You didn't reply to me at all.

699
00:34:59,670 --> 00:35:01,230
Didn't you miss Praewa even a little?

700
00:35:01,720 --> 00:35:03,320
I got shot.

701
00:35:03,980 --> 00:35:04,780
Where did you get shot?

702
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:06,220
Here, or right here?

703
00:35:07,060 --> 00:35:08,710
Is it here or here?

704
00:35:08,910 --> 00:35:10,520
Or maybe right here?

705
00:35:12,090 --> 00:35:12,790
It hurts a lot.

706
00:35:13,430 --> 00:35:15,350
I'm so sorry. I didn't know.

707
00:35:15,370 --> 00:35:17,410
If I knew,
I would've been there for you.

708
00:35:17,930 --> 00:35:19,780
But it's okay,
I'll take care of you right now.

709
00:35:19,810 --> 00:35:20,700
Your arm hurts, right?

710
00:35:20,730 --> 00:35:21,930
Let Praewa feed you.

711
00:35:21,960 --> 00:35:23,600
Just a second, don't eat yet.

712
00:35:25,730 --> 00:35:26,480
Look at you.

713
00:35:26,910 --> 00:35:28,670
- One khao soi, please.
- You're missing out on a real catch.

714
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,940
She's Sinthawee's niece, you know.

715
00:35:32,160 --> 00:35:33,410
It's not like I'm into her or anything.

716
00:35:33,510 --> 00:35:34,130
Wait.

717
00:35:34,420 --> 00:35:36,060
Even if you weren't into them before,
you'd still talk to them.

718
00:35:36,270 --> 00:35:37,800
Or did you already find the one?

719
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:39,500
Are you done playing games?

720
00:35:39,770 --> 00:35:40,870
A player like me...

721
00:35:41,710 --> 00:35:42,770
never stops.

722
00:35:45,670 --> 00:35:47,010
I'm going to go get some drinks.

723
00:35:50,970 --> 00:35:52,680
Sh*t, which side was I hurt on again?

724
00:35:52,710 --> 00:35:53,880
- Left, sir. Left.
- The left side.

725
00:35:53,970 --> 00:35:55,260
- Left, left, left.
- Left. It's the left one.

726
00:35:55,490 --> 00:35:57,180
I'm back, Thear.

727
00:35:59,450 --> 00:36:01,430
Easy there.
It really hurts right here.

728
00:36:01,460 --> 00:36:03,390
It's okay. I will take care of you.

729
00:36:03,640 --> 00:36:05,690
Honestly, I'm almost done with my bowl.

730
00:36:05,750 --> 00:36:08,270
You're recovering,
so you need to eat a lot.

731
00:36:13,450 --> 00:36:15,990
Good boy.

732
00:36:18,070 --> 00:36:18,870
Oh!

733
00:36:19,460 --> 00:36:20,440
Whose cat is this?

734
00:36:21,450 --> 00:36:22,600
So cute.

735
00:36:28,230 --> 00:36:28,680
Here.

736
00:36:31,020 --> 00:36:32,090
Yummy, yummy.

737
00:36:32,160 --> 00:36:34,140
Good job.

738
00:36:35,590 --> 00:36:36,960
I'll feed you more.

739
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,880
You're cute.

740
00:36:44,270 --> 00:36:46,630
Hey, Thear. There are people here.

741
00:36:47,820 --> 00:36:49,140
I'm gonna play with the cat for a bit.

742
00:36:49,170 --> 00:36:50,480
That cat over there is really cute.

743
00:36:51,550 --> 00:36:52,380
Thear...

744
00:36:53,070 --> 00:36:53,870
Thear.

745
00:36:54,370 --> 00:36:55,150
Thear.

746
00:36:55,340 --> 00:36:56,310
Thear.

747
00:36:56,340 --> 00:36:58,300
Thear, I have a cat at my place.

748
00:36:58,990 --> 00:36:59,830
Hey.

749
00:37:01,310 --> 00:37:02,380
That cat is so cute.

750
00:37:03,420 --> 00:37:04,170
Where did it come from?

751
00:37:04,210 --> 00:37:06,010
It's probably one of the vendors' cats
around here.

752
00:37:08,060 --> 00:37:09,280
Do you have that with you?

753
00:37:09,470 --> 00:37:10,720
What's that? Cat treats?

754
00:37:11,030 --> 00:37:13,470
I see stray cats all the time,
so I always keep some on me.

755
00:37:14,020 --> 00:37:16,150
And they're easy to carry around.

756
00:37:16,220 --> 00:37:18,720
Can I have one?
I'll feed a stray cat too if I see one.

757
00:37:21,780 --> 00:37:22,810
Oh, wait, I forgot.

758
00:37:23,270 --> 00:37:25,860
Praewa probably fed you
until you were full.

759
00:37:26,930 --> 00:37:27,730
You don't need any more food.

760
00:37:32,120 --> 00:37:33,320
Being this soft,

761
00:37:33,770 --> 00:37:35,260
can you really interrogate a suspect?

762
00:37:35,830 --> 00:37:37,010
Interrogate a suspect?

763
00:37:37,620 --> 00:37:38,630
Are you serious, Inspector?

764
00:37:39,130 --> 00:37:41,740
We've gotta put
our new member to the test.

765
00:37:58,720 --> 00:37:59,850
Go on, get in.

766
00:38:02,780 --> 00:38:03,940
Take a seat.

767
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:13,590
We'll have a casual talk.

768
00:38:24,440 --> 00:38:26,080
Isn't that a bit too casual?

769
00:38:26,410 --> 00:38:27,690
Show some respect to the officers.

770
00:38:27,710 --> 00:38:29,810
We're in full uniform
and mean business.

771
00:38:33,540 --> 00:38:35,110
I'll get straight to the point.

772
00:38:36,100 --> 00:38:38,450
Based on the evidence found at your house,

773
00:38:38,800 --> 00:38:40,640
there's not enough
to suggest that you're the leader.

774
00:38:40,930 --> 00:38:43,210
We've found links to this network
in several other provinces

775
00:38:43,350 --> 00:38:44,850
So just give it to me straight.

776
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:47,080
Who's your boss?

777
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:54,000
Just tell us who the leader is.

778
00:38:55,320 --> 00:38:56,400
You'd better cooperate.

779
00:38:58,920 --> 00:38:59,640
Hey!

780
00:38:59,950 --> 00:39:01,690
Answer the question, you piece of sh*t.

781
00:39:02,800 --> 00:39:04,950
Take it easy. I'll handle this myself.

782
00:39:06,910 --> 00:39:07,940
Listen up.

783
00:39:08,540 --> 00:39:10,550
You've been to prison before.
You know it's no joke.

784
00:39:10,970 --> 00:39:12,680
Taking the fall for your boss

785
00:39:13,040 --> 00:39:14,450
while he's out there living it up?

786
00:39:14,740 --> 00:39:15,990
You're the one who's going to suffer.

787
00:39:16,300 --> 00:39:17,540
The food there is trash anyway.

788
00:39:17,630 --> 00:39:19,220
But if you cooperate with us

789
00:39:20,240 --> 00:39:21,560
I can help you out.

790
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:23,480
We can get your sentence reduced.

791
00:39:23,790 --> 00:39:24,590
Trust me.

792
00:39:28,380 --> 00:39:30,170
I can do this all day.

793
00:39:31,800 --> 00:39:34,310
Let's see which one of us
can be more of a smart-ass.

794
00:39:43,600 --> 00:39:44,430
Inspector.

795
00:39:45,560 --> 00:39:46,990
Could you let me talk to him?

796
00:39:48,180 --> 00:39:49,910
I think I have a way.

797
00:39:53,510 --> 00:39:54,620
Is this actually going to work?

798
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:57,010
He's too soft for this.

799
00:39:57,130 --> 00:39:58,690
And that prick is being a real pain.

800
00:39:58,860 --> 00:39:59,480
Hey.

801
00:39:59,920 --> 00:40:02,040
Acting tough doesn't always work.

802
00:40:02,340 --> 00:40:04,040
This bastard isn't scared of you.

803
00:40:04,280 --> 00:40:05,850
Maybe we should try a softer approach.

804
00:40:06,190 --> 00:40:07,540
It might actually work.

805
00:40:09,930 --> 00:40:11,410
Let him show us what he's got.

806
00:40:11,440 --> 00:40:12,840
He's got potential. I've seen it before.

807
00:40:13,570 --> 00:40:14,700
When did you ever see that?

808
00:40:15,440 --> 00:40:17,820
Back when I was sent to train
the rookies with Phuwin.

809
00:40:19,060 --> 00:40:20,870
But I don't know
how he's doing lately.

810
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:22,330
Well, just wait and see.

811
00:40:26,670 --> 00:40:29,200
You wanna drink something sweet?

812
00:40:29,800 --> 00:40:31,380
Interrogations can be stressful.

813
00:40:31,480 --> 00:40:32,950
I don't want you to faint.

814
00:40:37,650 --> 00:40:39,230
Are you from Phayao?

815
00:40:39,830 --> 00:40:41,720
Why did you end up
working in Chiang Mai?

816
00:40:42,580 --> 00:40:44,680
I'm actually from Phayao too.

817
00:40:44,970 --> 00:40:47,360
I only moved to Chiang Mai recently.

818
00:40:48,260 --> 00:40:50,470
You're actually my very first case.

819
00:40:50,870 --> 00:40:52,240
Feeling homesick, right?

820
00:40:53,360 --> 00:40:55,350
It may not be as developed as here,

821
00:40:55,590 --> 00:40:56,970
but it still feels like home.

822
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:01,710
Oh, so where did you go to school?

823
00:41:05,120 --> 00:41:06,900
Phayao Municipal School 3.

824
00:41:07,590 --> 00:41:08,390
Whoa.

825
00:41:10,130 --> 00:41:11,800
We went to the same school.

826
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:13,560
You're my senior, you know that?

827
00:41:13,980 --> 00:41:15,410
I went to high school there.

828
00:41:17,240 --> 00:41:19,420
But that dean of students
was freaking strict, wasn't he?

829
00:41:19,670 --> 00:41:22,390
He was so strict.
I was terrified of him back then.

830
00:41:22,420 --> 00:41:23,940
He was the only one I was scared of.

831
00:41:26,360 --> 00:41:28,380
See? I told you.

832
00:41:29,150 --> 00:41:30,590
He's got the skills.

833
00:41:30,640 --> 00:41:32,570
That's my boy.
I trained him with my own hands.

834
00:41:33,280 --> 00:41:33,820
Yeah.

835
00:41:34,750 --> 00:41:35,940
You mean Lerm?

836
00:41:36,190 --> 00:41:38,390
Yeah, that Lerm guy.

837
00:41:38,410 --> 00:41:40,750
He was so old.

838
00:41:40,930 --> 00:41:42,600
But when he swung that cane

839
00:41:44,110 --> 00:41:45,750
my butt went completely numb.

840
00:41:45,870 --> 00:41:49,160
That's Lerm, the Punisher from Hell.

841
00:41:49,180 --> 00:41:50,620
That was what people call him.

842
00:41:51,720 --> 00:41:53,260
Missing the good old school days, huh?

843
00:42:02,210 --> 00:42:03,170
Go ahead, drink up.

844
00:42:06,350 --> 00:42:07,890
I really miss our school.

845
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:18,350
♪Phayao Municipal School 3♪

846
00:42:18,370 --> 00:42:22,410
♪Uniting our hearts as we move forward♪

847
00:42:26,930 --> 00:42:29,880
♪Wisdom leads us toward
a brighter future♪

848
00:42:29,940 --> 00:42:36,760
- ♪Toward a prosperous new day♪
- ♪Toward a prosperous new day♪

849
00:42:36,840 --> 00:42:40,110
You're my school senior.

850
00:42:40,300 --> 00:42:43,190
See? That's my boy, I told you.

851
00:42:43,290 --> 00:42:44,060
What the hell?

852
00:42:44,700 --> 00:42:47,330
Remember this.
It might come in handy.

853
00:42:48,600 --> 00:42:50,020
He went with the school anthem.

854
00:42:50,430 --> 00:42:51,960
I'm your junior.

855
00:42:52,710 --> 00:42:53,440
This is so unbelievable.

856
00:42:53,470 --> 00:42:55,630
You graduated so long ago
and you still remember the lyrics.

857
00:42:56,370 --> 00:42:58,620
I'm thinking of sending my kid there too.

858
00:42:59,600 --> 00:43:01,460
And what's your kid's name?

859
00:43:08,280 --> 00:43:09,640
His name is Rakpong.

860
00:43:09,820 --> 00:43:11,150
It's been a long time since
we last saw each other.

861
00:43:11,270 --> 00:43:12,950
I never fail to send him money.

862
00:43:12,970 --> 00:43:19,260
But I think after today,
it'll be a long time until we meet again.

863
00:43:28,680 --> 00:43:29,360
Hey.

864
00:43:30,740 --> 00:43:33,380
I can help you see your son sooner.

865
00:43:36,180 --> 00:43:38,110
But you have to give us something.

866
00:43:41,450 --> 00:43:43,130
I can't say it.

867
00:43:43,620 --> 00:43:44,850
Yes, you can.

868
00:43:44,920 --> 00:43:46,240
You're my senior.

869
00:43:46,740 --> 00:43:48,230
I'm your junior.

870
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:49,740
Trust me.

871
00:43:50,200 --> 00:43:53,120
I'll do everything I can
so you can see your kid again.

872
00:43:53,720 --> 00:43:54,480
Trust me.

873
00:43:58,010 --> 00:43:58,820
Please.

874
00:44:07,820 --> 00:44:08,630
Just tell me.

875
00:44:18,330 --> 00:44:19,260
- Sh*t!
- Sh*t! Get in there!

876
00:44:24,710 --> 00:44:26,040
Mungkorn, are you okay?

877
00:44:26,130 --> 00:44:27,000
I'm fine.

878
00:44:27,630 --> 00:44:30,140
You bastard.
You want me to get rough with you, huh?

879
00:44:34,890 --> 00:44:35,600
Inspector!

880
00:44:40,370 --> 00:44:41,170
Are you alright?

881
00:44:49,620 --> 00:44:51,630
Sh*t, what's wrong with him?

882
00:44:53,290 --> 00:44:54,970
Is this the same old trick?

883
00:44:57,870 --> 00:44:59,370
Get a doctor!

884
00:44:59,440 --> 00:45:00,080
Get a doctor now.

885
00:45:03,810 --> 00:45:05,340
Hey! Wake up!

886
00:45:13,200 --> 00:45:14,390
Dammit!

887
00:45:21,580 --> 00:45:22,590
He's dead.

888
00:45:30,980 --> 00:45:32,150
Just a little bit.

889
00:45:32,190 --> 00:45:33,240
What do you mean by "a little bit"?

890
00:45:33,680 --> 00:45:34,830
I mean it's only a little bit painful.

891
00:45:35,670 --> 00:45:36,480
Okay.

892
00:45:36,600 --> 00:45:37,150
Yes.

893
00:45:40,280 --> 00:45:42,090
You have such a charming way
of dressing wounds.

894
00:45:42,730 --> 00:45:45,200
Oh my, thank you.

895
00:45:45,230 --> 00:45:46,300
Please look straight ahead.

896
00:45:46,400 --> 00:45:48,160
If I look straight,
how can I see your face?

897
00:45:49,930 --> 00:45:51,870
Am I going to turn into a zombie

898
00:45:51,900 --> 00:45:52,820
after getting bitten like this?

899
00:45:52,900 --> 00:45:54,610
Definitely not.

900
00:45:54,640 --> 00:45:55,530
Look,

901
00:45:56,120 --> 00:45:58,330
the wound's been cleaned.
There won't be any infection.

902
00:45:58,360 --> 00:45:59,780
You can go home today.

903
00:45:59,830 --> 00:46:04,910
Please keep the wound area
away from water for a while.

904
00:46:04,970 --> 00:46:06,240
Do I really have to go home today?

905
00:46:06,270 --> 00:46:08,110
- Yes.
- Can't I stay for one more night?

906
00:46:08,470 --> 00:46:09,400
I want you to dress my wound again.

907
00:46:09,430 --> 00:46:12,130
I'll let him take care of you at home.

908
00:46:12,430 --> 00:46:13,490
I'll leave him in your hands.

909
00:46:13,600 --> 00:46:15,360
- Thank you very much.
- You're welcome.

910
00:46:16,910 --> 00:46:17,540
Hey.

911
00:46:18,760 --> 00:46:21,470
You could be charged
with harassing an officer.

912
00:46:22,040 --> 00:46:23,870
With a wound like that,
you're still hitting on her?

913
00:46:24,450 --> 00:46:25,250
Hey, you.

914
00:46:25,850 --> 00:46:28,470
You can't be jealous of everyone I meet.

915
00:46:29,470 --> 00:46:31,200
You keep saying that I get jealous.

916
00:46:31,400 --> 00:46:33,730
If a dog, a cat, or even a mosquito
gets close to you,

917
00:46:34,340 --> 00:46:35,510
am I supposed to
get jealous of them too?

918
00:46:37,290 --> 00:46:38,770
I'm just worried.

919
00:46:39,580 --> 00:46:40,800
Look at you now.

920
00:46:41,590 --> 00:46:42,710
You should know your limits.

921
00:46:44,230 --> 00:46:45,710
You're nagging me like this...

922
00:46:46,890 --> 00:46:48,230
Does it mean

923
00:46:49,740 --> 00:46:51,660
you've actually fallen for me?

924
00:46:53,420 --> 00:46:54,470
Come on, am I right?

925
00:46:55,340 --> 00:46:56,990
You're talking nonsense.

926
00:46:57,860 --> 00:46:58,660
Whoa.

927
00:46:59,840 --> 00:47:00,620
You good?

928
00:47:02,210 --> 00:47:03,080
I'm fine, buddy.

929
00:47:03,310 --> 00:47:04,110
I'm not dead yet.

930
00:47:06,570 --> 00:47:08,270
Orders came down from the higher-ups.

931
00:47:08,690 --> 00:47:10,210
You've been temporarily suspended.

932
00:47:10,760 --> 00:47:12,910
Right now, people say...

933
00:47:12,930 --> 00:47:14,740
you beat the suspect to death.

934
00:47:14,810 --> 00:47:15,870
They want you off the job

935
00:47:15,890 --> 00:47:17,200
pending further investigation.

936
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:18,730
What did I even do?

937
00:47:18,990 --> 00:47:20,700
I was just defending myself, wasn't I?

938
00:47:20,860 --> 00:47:22,820
And he just had a seizure.

939
00:47:22,960 --> 00:47:25,160
Then he died.
It's not like I killed him.

940
00:47:25,440 --> 00:47:26,870
Yeah, I know.

941
00:47:27,940 --> 00:47:31,560
But I'll follow up on
the autopsy report for you.

942
00:47:32,200 --> 00:47:34,100
Something about this feels off.

943
00:47:34,260 --> 00:47:34,790
Right.

944
00:47:35,730 --> 00:47:36,960
I'm counting on you.

945
00:47:38,940 --> 00:47:40,360
Here we go again, Theartha.

946
00:47:40,860 --> 00:47:41,630
Mom?

947
00:47:42,740 --> 00:47:45,880
Thear, I think you're in more trouble.

948
00:47:47,080 --> 00:47:47,690
Hello.

949
00:47:48,430 --> 00:47:49,100
I'm off now.

950
00:47:49,580 --> 00:47:51,200
Why did this have to happen again?

951
00:47:51,320 --> 00:47:53,430
Did you do everything I told you?

952
00:47:53,880 --> 00:47:56,260
Mom, I just got bitten.

953
00:47:56,280 --> 00:47:58,100
Then why are you still so unlucky?

954
00:47:59,620 --> 00:48:00,300
Wait.

955
00:48:01,840 --> 00:48:02,970
Is it possible...

956
00:48:04,060 --> 00:48:07,140
that you two haven't done
everything exactly

957
00:48:07,640 --> 00:48:09,210
as the oracle told you?

958
00:48:12,700 --> 00:48:13,380
Mom.

959
00:48:13,830 --> 00:48:17,720
I did every single thing you told me.

960
00:48:20,600 --> 00:48:21,500
We did everything.

961
00:48:22,680 --> 00:48:24,600
Something must be missing.

962
00:48:30,470 --> 00:48:32,070
- "Become one in the most intimate way."
- "Become one in the most intimate way."

963
00:48:35,320 --> 00:48:36,080
What was that?

964
00:48:41,180 --> 00:48:43,310
How naive of you.

965
00:48:43,520 --> 00:48:45,470
The oracle said

966
00:48:45,510 --> 00:48:50,040
that you two must
become one in the most intimate way.

967
00:48:50,170 --> 00:48:52,430
That's the only way to break the curse.

968
00:48:53,220 --> 00:48:55,920
And what is that supposed to mean?

969
00:48:58,500 --> 00:49:00,300
Well,

970
00:49:01,140 --> 00:49:03,000
isn't obvious?

971
00:49:03,400 --> 00:49:07,170
It's something you can do only with him.

972
00:49:08,150 --> 00:49:08,710
Huh?

973
00:49:12,790 --> 00:49:14,990
So, becoming one in the most intimate way...

974
00:49:15,950 --> 00:49:19,570
What's going to make you two
feel physically intimate?

975
00:49:22,420 --> 00:49:25,740
Let's just say it's a major mission.

976
00:49:26,690 --> 00:49:31,210
And the two of us must do it together.

977
00:49:32,070 --> 00:49:33,640
I'm begging you.

978
00:49:34,540 --> 00:49:40,550
Otherwise, this curse
will haunt you forever.

979
00:49:41,090 --> 00:49:42,450
Do we really have to do this?

980
00:49:42,650 --> 00:49:43,550
Yes.

981
00:50:10,980 --> 00:50:12,580
Isn't this a bit too much for me?

982
00:50:17,760 --> 00:50:19,430
Be patient with hurtful feelings.

983
00:50:19,950 --> 00:50:21,670
Endure difficulties.

984
00:50:22,900 --> 00:50:23,640
I can do this.

985
00:50:27,590 --> 00:50:29,030
Go for it, Phuwin.

986
00:50:29,500 --> 00:50:30,470
You've got this.

987
00:50:33,380 --> 00:50:35,130
Oh, Mungkorn.

988
00:50:35,370 --> 00:50:36,930
I miss you. What's up?

989
00:50:37,030 --> 00:50:38,050
Are you free right now?

990
00:50:38,600 --> 00:50:40,090
I need some advice.

991
00:50:40,330 --> 00:50:42,340
(I'm watching Phuwin right now.)

992
00:50:42,570 --> 00:50:44,100
(But for you, I'm always free.)

993
00:50:45,070 --> 00:50:46,000
The thing is...

994
00:50:47,070 --> 00:50:49,510
when two men do things together,

995
00:50:49,530 --> 00:50:51,310
how does it feel?

996
00:50:52,180 --> 00:50:53,490
Why are you asking?

997
00:50:57,650 --> 00:51:00,370
There's a case I need to research.

998
00:51:00,390 --> 00:51:02,910
So I'm just curious.

999
00:51:06,260 --> 00:51:07,070
Well...

1000
00:51:07,650 --> 00:51:10,780
It hurts a little the first time,

1001
00:51:11,580 --> 00:51:12,710
but it feels heartwarming,

1002
00:51:13,100 --> 00:51:13,890
like...

1003
00:51:14,470 --> 00:51:16,030
having all the love in the world.

1004
00:51:17,390 --> 00:51:19,140
So, how do you do it?

1005
00:51:22,200 --> 00:51:24,430
(Have you ever watched porn?)

1006
00:51:26,030 --> 00:51:27,310
I've never watched it.

1007
00:51:28,170 --> 00:51:28,970
I've been too busy.

1008
00:51:29,770 --> 00:51:32,500
(Mungkorn, really? At your age?)

1009
00:51:33,260 --> 00:51:35,120
(You should watch it
for educational purposes.)

1010
00:51:35,960 --> 00:51:37,520
(When I did it for the first time,)

1011
00:51:37,540 --> 00:51:39,570
(I just followed those videos.)

1012
00:51:39,680 --> 00:51:42,890
(But in the end, if both people
want to make each other happy,)

1013
00:51:43,070 --> 00:51:44,740
(they'll find a way.)

1014
00:51:51,840 --> 00:51:53,070
I'm exhausted, Lukplub.

1015
00:51:53,420 --> 00:51:55,380
(Oh, Mungkorn.)

1016
00:51:55,610 --> 00:51:57,040
(How are you doing? Everything good?)

1017
00:51:57,520 --> 00:51:58,800
I'm doing well.

1018
00:51:59,670 --> 00:52:03,450
(Good luck with your secret mission.)

1019
00:52:03,510 --> 00:52:05,000
(Tell me how it turns out.)

1020
00:52:05,120 --> 00:52:05,900
Okay.

1021
00:52:06,840 --> 00:52:08,720
It's not like
I'm actually going to do it.

1022
00:52:25,450 --> 00:52:26,740
(Pizza delivery.)

1023
00:52:27,040 --> 00:52:29,120
(Uh, hold on a second.)

1024
00:52:29,660 --> 00:52:31,490
(I'm out of cash.)

1025
00:52:31,600 --> 00:52:32,890
(You can pay me in other ways.)

1026
00:52:33,360 --> 00:52:34,560
(Pay with what?)

1027
00:53:07,780 --> 00:53:09,470
I'm ready to be yours, Inspector.

1028
00:53:12,810 --> 00:53:14,010
What's gotten into you?

1029
00:53:19,510 --> 00:53:21,740
What is the secret
between the two of you?

1030
00:53:21,760 --> 00:53:23,130
There really was nothing.

1031
00:53:24,610 --> 00:53:26,310
What exactly am I to you?

1032
00:53:26,340 --> 00:53:28,440
You should take Mungkorn
back home for a visit.

1033
00:53:28,500 --> 00:53:31,570
If there's any misunderstanding,
talk it out.

1034
00:53:31,680 --> 00:53:33,740
Anyone who gets close to me
ends up falling for me.

1035
00:53:33,770 --> 00:53:35,740
I never miss a target I set my sight on.

1036
00:53:39,550 --> 00:53:41,530
I think the only thing
you're truly an expert at

1037
00:53:42,260 --> 00:53:44,290
is imagining things.

1038
00:53:46,540 --> 00:53:51,450
♪Trying so hard not to cross the line,♪

1039
00:53:51,480 --> 00:53:56,310
♪But the more I run,
the more you're on my mind♪

1040
00:53:56,340 --> 00:54:00,610
♪If you're gonna love me,
don't break the deal we made♪

1041
00:54:00,640 --> 00:54:06,160
♪Don't break my heart,
remember what you said?♪

1042
00:54:06,190 --> 00:54:11,060
♪Let's call off the deal
and let our hearts decide♪

1043
00:54:11,090 --> 00:54:17,520
♪From contracting parties to lovers,
does that sound alright?♪

1044
00:54:23,720 --> 00:54:26,920
♪It's time you became mine♪
